# qmldir — explicit module manifest for quickshell/modules/settings/ (quick
# task 260820-sqd, Task 1). Mirrors every sibling module manifest's own
# standing instruction (modules/qmldir:1-11): checking this file in disables
# Quickshell's directory-scanner synthesis for this directory entirely — any
# .qml type added here that is NOT declared below becomes unresolvable
# forever, with no load error. Any FUTURE type added to this directory MUST
# be declared in the same commit that creates it.
#
# PageRegistry/PageCompRegistry carry BOTH `pragma Singleton` in their own
# file AND the `singleton` keyword here — modules/qmldir:14-21's
# binary-verified finding: without the qmldir keyword, bare
# `PageRegistry.pages`-style access resolves to `undefined` forever (the
# object is never constructed). SettingsState is deliberately NOT a
# singleton (one instance per window, owned by Settings.qml).
module qs.modules.settings
singleton PageRegistry 1.0 PageRegistry.qml
singleton PageCompRegistry 1.0 PageCompRegistry.qml
SettingsState 1.0 SettingsState.qml
NavRail 1.0 NavRail.qml
Pages 1.0 Pages.qml
Settings 1.0 Settings.qml
